",primals_tertiary_just:\"Just vs. Unjust\",primals_secondary_enticing:\"Enticing vs. Dull\",primals_tertiary_interesting:\"Interesting vs. Boring\",primals_tertiary_beautiful:\"Beautiful vs. Ugly\",primals_tertiary_abundant:\"Abundant vs. Barren\",primals_tertiary_worthexploring:\"Worth Exploring vs. Not Worth Exploring\",primals_tertiary_meaningful:\"Meaningful vs. Meaningless\",primals_tertiary_improvable:\"Improvable vs. Too Hard to Improve\",primals_tertiary_funny:\"Funny vs. Not Funny\",primals_secondary_alive:\"Alive vs. Mechanistic\",primals_tertiary_intentional:\"Intentional vs. Unintentional\",primals_tertiary_needsme:\"Needs Me vs. Doesn’t Need Me\",primals_tertiary_interactive:\"Interactive vs. Indifferent\",primals_tertiary_acceptable:\"Acceptable vs. Unacceptable\",primals_tertiary_changing:\"Changing vs. Static\",primals_tertiary_hierarchical:\"Hierarchical vs. Nonhierarchical\",primals_tertiary_interconnected:\"Interconnected vs. Separable\",primals_tertiary_understandable:\"Understandable vs. Too Hard to Understand\"},scaleDescriptions:{primals_primary_good:\"Belief that the world is fundamentally good\",primals_secondary_safe:\"The Safe vs. Dangerous dimension captures your views about the world being a threatening place. More specifically, this dimension reflects your responses to statements about the world being fair (vs. unfair), comfortable (or not), (un)stable, and malignant or benign. Higher scores indicate a greater belief that the world is safe and lower scores that the world is more dangerous.\",primals_tertiary_pleasurable:\"Belief that most aspects of the world are (hedonically) pleasing\",primals_tertiary_regenerative:\"Belief that the world tends to repair and heal itself rather than decay\",primals_tertiary_progressing:\"Belief that the world is improving over time rather than getting worse\",primals_tertiary_harmless:\"Belief that most aspects of the world are not very dangerous\",primals_tertiary_cooperative:\"Belief that the world is mostly cooperative and collaborative instead of competitive\",primals_tertiary_stable:\"Belief that the world is stable and resilient instead of fragile and frail\",primals_tertiary_just:\"Belief that the world is generally fair instead of unfair\",primals_secondary_enticing:\"The Enticing vs. Dull dimension reflects one’s interest in engaging with the world. How much do you find it worth exploring—full of beauty, meaning, and interesting opportunities or perhaps the opposite? High scores indicate a greater belief that the world is enticing.\",primals_tertiary_interesting:\"Belief that the world is full of fascinating and intellectually engaging things\",primals_tertiary_beautiful:\"Belief that the world is full of aesthetically interesting, and even beautiful, things\",primals_tertiary_abundant:\"Belief that the world is full of resources and opportunities\",primals_tertiary_worthexploring:\"Belief that the world is full of interesting experiences worth discovering\",primals_tertiary_meaningful:\"Belief that the objects and events in our world have deep meaning\",primals_tertiary_improvable:\"Belief that most aspects of the world can be changed for the better\",primals_tertiary_funny:\"Belief that the world offers many opportunities for humor and laughter\",primals_secondary_alive:\"The Alive vs. Mechanistic dimension captures beliefs about the extent to which each person’s experience of life is shaped (or not) by their behavior and intentions. Higher scores suggest a greater belief that things happen for a reason, and that each person serves an important purpose. Lower scores suggest an opinion that events occur at random, at least to some extent, and that the universe is generally unaffected by the actions of each individual.\",primals_tertiary_intentional:\"Belief that most things happen for a reason\",primals_tertiary_needsme:\"Belief that the world needs you for some specific (perhaps unique) purpose\",primals_tertiary_interactive:\"Belief that circumstances of the world react, in part, based on your influences\",primals_tertiary_acceptable:\"Belief that most things in the world are best accepted as they are\",primals_tertiary_changing:\"Belief that the world is ever-changing vs. constant\",primals_tertiary_hierarchical:\"Belief that most things in the world can be ordered or ranked vs. not\",primals_tertiary_interconnected:\"Belief that most aspects of the world are inter-related vs. independent\",primals_tertiary_understandable:\"Belief that most aspects of the world can be understood (or not)\"},scaleDescriptionsShort:{primals_secondary_safe:\"Belief that the world is safe\",primals_secondary_enticing:\"Belief that the world is enticing\",primals_secondary_alive:\"Belief that things happen for a reason\",primals_tertiary_understandable:\"Belief that most aspects of the world can be understood\",primals_tertiary_hierarchical:\"Belief that most things in the world can be ordered or ranked\",primals_tertiary_interconnected:\"Belief that most aspects of the world are inter-related\",primals_tertiary_changing:\"Belief that the world is ever-changing\",primals_tertiary_stable:\"Belief that the world is stable and resilient\",primals_tertiary_regenerative:\"Belief that the world tends to repair and heal itself\",primals_tertiary_progressing:\"Belief that the world is improving over time\"}};var lb={primals_primary_good:[2.464788732,2.704225352,2.845070423,2.943661972,3.042253521,3.112676056,3.183098592,3.23943662,3.281690141,3.338028169,3.38028169,3.408450704,3.450704225,3.478873239,3.521126761,3.549295775,3.577464789,3.605633803,3.61971831,3.647887324,3.676056338,3.704225352,3.718309859,3.746478873,3.76056338,3.788732394,3.802816901,3.816901408,3.845070423,3.85915493,3.873239437,3.901408451,3.915492958,3.929577465,3.943661972,3.971830986,3.985915493,4,4.014084507,4.028169014,4.042253521,4.070422535,4.084507042,4.098591549,4.112676056,4.126760563,4.14084507,4.154929577,4.169014085,4.183098592,4.211267606,4.225352113,4.239